{{also|lif}}
==Icelandic==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|non|is}} {{m|non|líf}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|is}} {{m|gem-pro|*lībą}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/liːv/|lang=is}}
*: {{rhymes|iːv|lang=is}}

===Noun===
{{is-noun|n|lífs|líf}}

# a [[life]]{{jump|is|life|s}}
#* ''Article 1'', [[Universal Declaration of Human Rights]] ([http://www.ohchr.org/EN/UDHR/Pages/Language.aspx?LangID=ice Icelandic], [http://www.ohchr.org/EN/UDHR/Pages/Language.aspx?LangID=eng English])
#*: ''Allir menn eiga rétt til '''lífs''', frelsis og mannhelgi.''
#*:: Everyone has the right to '''life''', liberty and security of person.
# {{lb|is|video games}} a [[life]], one of the [[player]]'s chances to play, lost when a mistake is made.
#: ''Ég fékk [[auka-|auka]]'''líf'''!''
#:: I got an extra '''life'''!

